
The Main Characters
Michael De Santa: A wealthy, retired bank robber living in witness protection with an unhappy family.
Franklin Clinton: A young street hustler looking for big money and a better life.
Trevor Philips: A violent, unpredictable psychopath and Michael's former criminal partner

The Plot
The story begins after a botched bank heist in 2004 where Michael fakes his own death.
 Years later in 2013, Michael crosses paths with Franklin, and the two team up for local criminal jobs.
When Michael pulls off a high-profile jewelry store robbery,
Trevor recognizes his old friend's style on television and tracks him down
Reunited, the trio gets forced by corrupt government agents
(from the FIB, a parody of the FBI)
to perform dangerous operations. To secure their own freedom and fortunes,
the three men plan and execute a series of massive, high-stakes bank heists.
